The sandbox half written as a profile of its own rather than as a mode.

`default_permissions` names a `[permissions.<name>]` table, and what that table
grants is read out of it: a filesystem rule for the workspace roots is a write,
so nothing asks and the agent may write.

>>> .codex/config.toml
approval_policy = "never"
default_permissions = "ours"

[permissions.ours]
description = "what our agents may touch"

[permissions.ours.filesystem.":workspace_roots"]
"." = "write"
